  "body": "Hi,\r\n\r\nMy goal is to setup usb gadget on raspberry pi zero and it is recognized and connected to webusb for application-specific communications.\r\n\r\nI did some research around and got lost in the jungle.  Would appreciate any pointers.\r\n\r\nI can easily setup CDC function on raspberry pi.  While it is recognized as serial port on windows and is functional through terminal apps such as putty, it is not recognized by webusb (chrome+windows 7/10).  What kind of devices would be recognized by webusb without a driver on windows?\r\n\r\nI was able to get some vendor specific USB gadget device recognized by webusb (via winusb.sys driver, I believe).  However, I'm not how to achieve this on the raspberry side with app-accessible endpoints.\r\n\r\nAgain, would appreciate any pointers!  I think I really need a direction.  Thanks! ",
